.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt QOBSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm qobsd
.Nd install, upgrade, and run OpenBSD guests under QEMU
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Op Fl f Ar image
.Op Fl H Ar hostname
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Ar arch
.Op Ar qemu-arg ...
.Nm
.Op Fl nk
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Op Fl f Ar image
.Op Fl H Ar hostname
.Pq Fl m | Fl i | Fl u
.Pq Fl s | Fl R Ar version
.Ar arch
.Op Ar installurl
.Op Ar qemu-arg ...
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl d Ar directory
.Op Fl f Ar image
.Fl z
.Ar arch
.Op Ar convert-arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no mode flag,
.Nm
boots an existing qcow2 disk with a serial console.
VM arguments after
.Ar arch
and any
.Ar installurl
pass to
.Xr qemu 1 .
.Pp
Supported architectures are
.Cm amd64 , arm64 , armv7 , hppa , i386 , macppc , octeon ,
.Cm powerpc64 , riscv64 ,
and
.Cm sparc64 .
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Fl d Ar directory
Set the working directory for relative paths.
.It Fl f Ar image
Set the disk image, defaulting to
.Ar arch Ns Pa .qcow2 .
.It Fl H Ar hostname
Set the guest hostname, defaulting to
.Li qobsd- Ns Ar arch Ns Li . Ns Ar host-hostname .
Short names use the host's hostname as their domain.
.It Fl i
Install unattended, creating the disk if needed.
.It Fl k
Skip host verification of installer files.
.It Fl m
Boot the interactive installer.
.It Fl n
Dry run, printing QEMU or conversion commands.
Snapshot media lookup may contact the mirror.
.It Fl p Ar port
Forward a host TCP port on all IPv4 interfaces to guest SSH.
.It Fl R Ar version
Use an OpenBSD release.
.It Fl s
Use an OpenBSD snapshot.
.It Fl u
Upgrade an existing disk unattended.
.It Fl z
Compact a stopped guest's disk, replacing it on success.
Pass
.Cm qemu-img convert
options after
.Ar arch ,
such as
.Fl c
for compression.
.El
.Ss Installation source
.Ar installurl
is a local directory or an FTP, HTTP, or HTTPS mirror containing
.Ar version Ns Pa / Ns Ar arch
or
.Pa snapshots/ Ns Ar arch .
The default is the first mirror in
.Pa @SYSCONFDIR@/installurl ,
falling back to
.Lk https://cdn.openbsd.org/pub/OpenBSD .
Select the distribution set source in the guest.
Installation and upgrade exit on guest reboot.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width DISK_SIZE -compact
.It Ev DISK_SIZE
New disk size, default
.Li 128G .
.It Ev TMPDIR
Temporary file directory, default
.Pa /tmp .
.El
.Sh FILES
Supply installation inputs together in the working directory.
If none are present, the defaults come from
.Pa @LOCALBASE@/share/examples/qobsd .
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width site.perms -compact
.It Pa install.conf
Answer file, required by
.Fl i
and
.Fl u ,
and to create a disk with
.Fl m .
.It Pa disklabel
Autopartitioning template, if referenced by
.Pa install.conf .
.It Pa site/ , site.perms
Optional site tree and
.Xr mtree 5
manifest, required together.
.Li contents=
paths are relative to
.Pa site/ .
.It Pa u-boot-octeon3-qobsd-boot.pflash
Octeon boot flash.
A local copy overrides the example.
.It Pa u-boot-octeon3-qobsd-install.pflash
Octeon installation flash.
Local flash images are writable.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
VM runs return QEMU's exit status.
Other invocations return 0 on success, 1 on failure, or 2 for invalid
usage.
.Sh EXAMPLES
With
.Pa install.conf
in the working directory, install an amd64 snapshot into a new image.
When installation finishes, boot the same image.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qobsd -f snapshot.qcow2 -i -s amd64
qobsd -f snapshot.qcow2 amd64
.Ed
.Pp
With the snapshot guest stopped, upgrade its disk to the current
snapshot.
.Dl qobsd -f snapshot.qcow2 -u -s amd64
.Pp
Boot an existing amd64 guest with 8G of RAM and forward host TCP port
2222 to guest SSH.
.Dl qobsd -f dev.qcow2 -p 2222 amd64 -m 8G
.Pp
Boot the OpenBSD 8.0 installer with an existing
.Pa macppc.qcow2
disk, using a local mirror with media under
.Pa /var/mirror/OpenBSD/8.0/macppc .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qobsd -m -R 8.0 macppc /var/mirror/OpenBSD
.Ed
.Pp
After shutting down the snapshot guest, compact its disk with
compression.
.Dl qobsd -f snapshot.qcow2 -z amd64 -c
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr qemu 1 ,
.Xr qemu-img 1 ,
.Xr installurl 5 ,
.Xr mtree 5 ,
.Xr autoinstall 8 ,
.Xr disklabel 8
.Sh CAVEATS
.Fl i
and
.Fl u
are unavailable on
.Cm hppa , macppc , powerpc64 ,
and
.Cm sparc64 .
If U-Boot starts the disk on
.Cm arm64 , armv7 ,
or
.Cm riscv64 ,
select network boot manually.
On
.Cm powerpc64 ,
select
.Dq OpenBSD install
in Petitboot if needed.
.Pp
.Cm macppc
supports at most 2G of RAM and one CPU.
On
.Cm octeon ,
match the CPU count to U-Boot's
.Cm numcores .
